@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: why a package exists for its exit-status types, how main turns them into proveo's exit code, and why the interface it was created for is never written
' covers: internal/backend/backend.go
' covers: internal/backend/backend_test.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/main.go (main, exitCode)
' covers: cmd/proveo/main_test.go (TestExitCodeIsTheAgentsOrTheStoppingSignals)
'   where a stop becomes Stopped .... _spec/internal/sbx/kit-lifecycle.puml
'   the transcript's outcome line .. _spec/internal/runlog/run-transcript.puml
'
' ── 2026-10-17: A SECOND TYPE, Stopped ─────────────────────────────────────
' The user, on a stopped run's exit status: "Exit 128+sig, 'stopped'
' (Recommended)". MEASURED, internal/backend/backend.go:
'   type Stopped struct{ Signal syscall.Signal }
'   Error() "stopped by SIGTERM" | "stopped by SIGHUP" | "stopped by signal N"
'   Code()  128 + signal → 143 for SIGTERM, 129 for SIGHUP
' internal/backend/sandbox Run returns Stopped when a forwarded SIGTERM/SIGHUP
' ended the run and the operator had not chosen Ctrl+C remove; teardown runs as
' on a normal exit. cmd/proveo main's exitCode(err) recovers ExitError → Code
' and Stopped → Code() through errors.As, and main calls os.Exit with it,
' printing nothing; any other error prints and exits 1. So a shell, CI step or
' the scheduler's `echo $? > <run>.exit` reads 143 for a stop, the status a
' shell reports for a process SIGTERM ended. A stop is neither success (0) nor
' proveo's own failure (1).
' Pinned by TestAStopExitsWith128PlusTheSignal (backend_test.go, through a %w
' wrap) and TestExitCodeIsTheAgentsOrTheStoppingSignals (main_test.go).
' COVERAGE CHOICE: cmd/proveo/main.go and main_test.go are covered here because
' main and exitCode turn the command's error into proveo's process status; a
' change there must flag this spec even though both files mostly hold unrelated
' commands. Expect drift reports from those unrelated edits too.
' The package-placement argument below applies to Stopped as it does to
' ExitError: internal/backend/sandbox builds it and cmd/proveo reads it.
' internal/run's recordOutcome only prints it (%v), through its default branch.
'
' ── 2026-10-16: ONE BACKEND LEFT ───────────────────────────────────────────
' internal/backend/dockeregress is DELETED with the docker+egress backend
' ("Retire Docker egress"); internal/backend/sandbox is the only consumer of
' ExitError besides cmd/proveo, and run.selectBackend became launchSandbox. The
' dependency-direction argument below weakens with one backend: placing
' ExitError inside internal/backend/sandbox no longer forces a sibling import.
' That move is repo-simplification.puml N16 (PROPOSED), not decided here.
' Everything below that names dockeregress or "both backends" is HISTORY.
'
' ── NO INTERFACE, AND THAT IS THE FINISHED STATE ───────────────────────────
' (Until 2026-10-17 the package held ONE type, ExitError; Stopped is the second.)
' The package was created during the cmd/proveo decomposition to hold what the
' two backends share, with a Plan(RunSpec)/Execute(Plan) interface promised once
' RunSpec existed. RunSpec now exists. THE INTERFACE IS STILL NOT WRITTEN, and
' the promise is withdrawn rather than left standing.
'
' Nothing consumes the backends polymorphically. run.selectBackend branches on
' which one won and calls each by name, because their shapes genuinely differ:
' sandbox.Run takes an Input and runs, while dockeregress splits into Assemble
' then Exec so the caller can start a review gate BETWEEN the two. An interface
' over two divergent implementers with no caller holding one describes nothing —
' it guesses a shape, which is the abstraction Go's own advice says to declare at
' the CONSUMER once a consumer exists.
'
' ── WHY THE PACKAGE STAYS ANYWAY ───────────────────────────────────────────
' Not for abstraction — for dependency direction. ExitError is needed by
' cmd/proveo and by BOTH backends. Put it in either backend and the other has to
' import its sibling; put it in cmd/proveo and internal/ imports cmd/. A leaf
' package is the only placement that leaves the graph acyclic.
'
' ── WHAT THE TYPE ACTUALLY GUARDS ──────────────────────────────────────────
' proveo's exit status must be the AGENT's, not proveo's own. A backend returns
' ExitError from deep inside a run and main recovers it with errors.As, so a CI
' step sees what the agent decided. The value must therefore survive wrapping:
' TestExitErrorSurvivesWrapping pins that, because a type that stopped matching
' through a %w chain would silently turn every agent failure into exit 1 and no
' test of the happy path would notice.
title internal/backend — a package for dependency direction, not abstraction

participant "sandbox" as SBX <<cloud>>
participant "backend.ExitError" as EE <<data>>
participant "backend.Stopped" as ST <<data>>
participant "cmd/proveo main\nexitCode" as MAIN <<app>>

SBX ARROW_ERROR EE : agent exited 137
EE ARROW_MAIN MAIN : errors.As through the wrap chain
MAIN ARROW_MAIN MAIN : os.Exit(code) — the AGENT's code
SBX ARROW_ERROR ST : forwarded SIGTERM/SIGHUP,\nnot the Ctrl+C remove path
ST ARROW_MAIN MAIN : errors.As through the wrap chain
MAIN ARROW_MAIN MAIN : os.Exit(128+signal) — 143 / 129

note over EE
  **No Plan/Execute interface.** One implementer
  since 2026-10-16 (dockeregress deleted), and no
  caller that holds one. Declared at the consumer,
  if a consumer ever appears.
end note

note over ST
  **A stop exits 128+signal, not 0 or 1.**
  143 for SIGTERM, 129 for SIGHUP: what a shell
  reports for a process the signal ended. main
  prints nothing for it, as for ExitError.
end note
@enduml
